prompt.text:
Implement a new mutable TypeScript buffer whose state can be safely imported and exported.

Export:

```typescript
export interface SegmentSnapshot {
    length: number;
    cells: readonly string[];
}

export class SegmentBuffer {
    constructor(length: number);
    readonly length: number;
    setRange(start: number, endExclusive: number, value: string): void;
    get(index: number): string;
    serialize(separator?: string): string;
    snapshot(): SegmentSnapshot;
    static fromSnapshot(snapshot: SegmentSnapshot): SegmentBuffer;
}
```

`length` must be a non-negative safe integer. New cells contain the empty string. Indices and range endpoints must be safe integers. `get` accepts only `0 <= index < length`. `setRange` requires `0 <= start <= endExclusive <= length`, writes exactly the half-open range, and treats an empty range as a no-op. Invalid numeric values or bounds throw `RangeError`; a non-string cell value or separator throws `TypeError`.

`serialize` joins all cells in index order, using `"|"` by default. For a zero-length buffer it returns the empty string. `snapshot` returns a new object and a new cell array. `fromSnapshot` validates the snapshot object, its length, exact cell count, and every string cell, then copies all data. Subsequent mutation of source or returned arrays must not affect the buffer.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

